```

Security decisions:
- Markdown conversion and DOMPurify sanitization run **server-side only**; the client receives already-sanitized HTML.
- The React component avoids `dangerouslySetInnerHTML` and uses DOM APIs that do not execute inline scripts, keeping it compatible with a nonce-based CSP.
- DOMPurify uses an explicit tag/attribute allowlist and blocks non-http(s) URL protocols.
- Dependencies are pinned exactly; `dompurify` (source: https://github.com/cure53/DOMPurify) and `marked` (source: https://github.com/markedjs/marked) are established packages.
